module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.committed_generated_artifact_absent_from_the_registry

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data committed_generated_artifact_absent_from_the_registry: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "committed_generated_artifact_absent_from_the_registry" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the capability of joining every committed file that sits at a gunbc.generated_artifact artifact_location against the artifact paths of generated_artifact_registry's members, and refusing a commit that leaves a file at a generated location with no member -- the same census gunbc.guarantee_stall.generated_artifact_registry_membership_stall names as its own retirement condition" } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a committed file emitted from a .dag authority has a variant in gunbc.generated_artifact (location, CommitRequired policy, producer row) and is absent from gunbc.generated_artifact_registry, so no consumer of committed_generated_artifacts adjudicates it and no required step can tell it from hand-authored source. HARM: generated bytes are committed, hand-edited and merge-conflicted on main while every consumer of the roster is green. DISTINGUISHING MARK: the file's .gitattributes entry is !merge, the hand-made setting, because the merge rows derive from the same roster that omits it (gunbc.gitattributes_emit deterministic_generated_projection_merge_rows) -- two carriers agreeing with each other and both disagreeing with the emitting authority.",

    "SPECIMEN ONE (this class, found by audit and not by any check): gunbc#15598 added InstrumentRegistryGeneratedRsArtifact with its committed location src/v1/stage0/src/instrument_registry_generated.rs, its CommitRequired policy, its producer row in gunbc.instruments.instrument_registry_emit (expected_instrument_registry_generated_rs) and its arms in the seed-build and docs-projection emits, and did not enter it into generated_artifact_registry. The file sat committed, watched by nothing, and .gitattributes carried it as !merge until the enrollment in gunbc#16129. Nothing went red at the introducing commit or at any commit after it: the artifact was never in the roster, so the projections never had a row of its to lose.",

    "SPECIMEN TWO, THE SAME OMISSION BY A DIFFERENT AUTHOR: gunbc#15995's own record states that native_route_seed_boundary_generated.rs 'sat in a generated location with NO entry: unproduced, unwatched, hand-editable by anyone, and its variant was never enrolled in generated_artifact_registry'. It was hand-written source in a generated location -- the file that the class above predicts -- and was retired into a producer only when its registry enrollment landed (gunbc.design_ruling :: seed_build_artifacts_must_be_regenerated_by_their_producer, ruling 3).",

    "THE POPULATION IS NOT EMPTY AND IS NOT EMPTY-BY-ACCIDENT: test.claim.regeneration_rosters_witness already asserts all(seed_build_artifacts(), a => committed_generated_artifact_paths() contains artifact_path(a)), so an artifact in the seed-build roster and not the registry is a located finding -- and it was RED while both specimens sat on main, in a corpus that gates nothing (the witnesses workflow ran neither on the PR that introduced them nor on this head). The class is not 'nobody thought to write the check'; it is 'the check exists and is not on a path anything must pass'.",

    "DISCRIMINATOR, MEASURED ON THE ENROLLMENT HEAD (gunbc run --claim-run, pinned v1 CLI, each run under an RSS watchdog): adding the one member to the registry list moves test.claim.gitattributes_emit_witness from 7/7 PASS at exit 0 (5m, peak RSS 3.29 GiB) to 6/7 with the single FAIL on witness_committed_matches_emit_holds at exit 1 (4m, peak RSS 3.29 GiB) -- the emitted .gitattributes gains the merge=generated-artifact row the committed file lacks. Removing it returns the witness to 7/7. So the enrollment's effect is observable, and the only thing that notices is that one claim.",

    "THE OTHER HALF OF THE MEASUREMENT IS WHY THIS ROW EXISTS ALONGSIDE THE STALL ROW IT CITES: the only writer of the committed projection is gunbc.instruments.generated_artifact_gate main_wet / main_wet_one, and four attempts at main_wet_one(path = '.gitattributes') on this head crossed the 12 GiB budget this host sets for local gate runs and were killed by the watchdog there -- exit 137 at peaks 12,585,060 / 12,586,112 / 12,591,792 / 12,588,028 KiB, 13m to 16m each -- and none of the three levers a reader would reach for held it under: MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2 (what the CI jobs set), a declared GUNBC_MEMORY_BUDGET_BYTES=10 GiB (the governor's ceiling is a planning request, not enforcement: its own arm says it 'may only request a LOWER planning ceiling', src/v1/stage0/src/memory_governor.rs), and GUNBC_EVAL_MEMO=0, which is documented as shedding the byte-unbounded call memo and is therefore a trade of time for memory -- it bought a slower run, not a smaller one. The gate module's comment still records a measured main_wet_one peak of 8.37 GiB, which is stale at this head by more than 50%. A repair whose only writer does not fit the budget of the session that found the defect is not a repair; the budget finding belongs to the ledger, not to a PR comment.",

    "HOW THE ENROLLMENT LANDED WITHOUT THE WRITER, AND WHAT PROVES IT IS THE AUTHORITY'S OWN BYTES: generated_artifact_gate main_wet_one could not run inside the budget, so the committed projection was brought to the emitter's output by applying the emitter's own two rules -- deterministic_generated_projection_paths() sorts committed_generated_artifact_paths(), so the new row enters the merge block between gunbc_file_transport_generated.rs and native_route_seed_boundary_generated.rs; and derived_hand_maintained_disposition_repo_paths() filters out any path in generated_artifact_stage0_src_repo_paths(), so the file's !merge row leaves the hand-maintained block. The equality is not argued from that reading: test.claim.gitattributes_emit_witness, which compares the committed bytes with expected_gitattributes(), went from 6/7 (the single FAIL on witness_committed_matches_emit_holds) to 7/7 PASS at exit 0 (4m, peak RSS 3.15 GiB). THE RESTORATION TRIGGER IS TYPED, NOT PROSE: it is this row's rung standing, and the drift this receipt describes was discharged by the claim going green with the member enrolled.",

    "WHERE A READER SHOULD LOOK FIRST, WHICH IS THE CHEAP DETECTOR: do not ask whether the file is generated -- ask whether it is in committed_generated_artifacts(). Join, in one instrument, the set of committed files sitting at a gunbc.generated_artifact artifact_location against the set of registry members' artifact paths, and refuse on any committed file at a generated location with no member. That census is also the retirement condition of gunbc.guarantee_stall.generated_artifact_registry_membership_stall, whose population is the five consumers that skip an absent member in agreement and whose blocker is that the census is unbuilt.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.generated_artifact_registry", decl_name: "committed_generated_artifacts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.generated_artifact", decl_name: "InstrumentRegistryGeneratedRsArtifact", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.seed_build_artifact_emit", decl_name: "seed_build_artifacts", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.gitattributes_emit", decl_name: "expected_gitattributes", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.instruments.generated_artifact_gate", decl_name: "main_wet_one", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.regeneration_rosters_witness", decl_name: "witness_every_seed_build_artifact_is_a_committed_registry_artifact", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "test.claim.gitattributes_emit_witness", decl_name: "witness_committed_matches_emit_holds", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.guarantee_stall.generated_artifact_registry_membership_stall", decl_name: "generated_artifact_registry_membership_stall", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
